note bottom of W7 #F1F5F9
  **Why W-7 heads the graph.** The declarative NativeEval forms are a **new identity**,
  not a v1-compatible refactor: ""identity.rs::write_language"" feeds all five <latex>\bigstar</latex> fields into
  the hashed identity as verbatim token text, so ""(&#34;op&#34;, &#34;add&#34;)"" and ""![a + b]"" //cannot//
  produce the same fingerprint. Bumping the prefix makes the transition explicit, versioned
  and diagnosable instead of a silent non-match under one prefix.

  What keeps v1 and v2 tags non-confusable is the **fixed OFFSET of the version digit**, not
  the fingerprint's length: ""mettail.term."" is 13 characters and ""mettail-langdef-v"" is 17,
  so the digit sits at tag index **30** in both generations, inside two fixed-width prefixes
  that no label can reach. A length argument would be invalid here — differing <latex>|\mathcal{F}|</latex> does //not//
  imply differing concatenations — and would rest version safety on the very property W-7
  changes.
end note

